
USAGE
        SYSop

DESCRIPTION
        Give a password challenge to get sysop's privileges:

        node> 3 7 1 12 5 [1795430000]

        Answer either with the characters of the password found at
        the 5 positions given (here the 3rd, 7th, 1st, 12th and 5th),
        or with the MD5 key of the number in brackets followed by the
        password. The password itself, typed in plain text, is refused:
        it would go on the air.

        On a Linux machine with FPAC, the fpacmd5 program works out the
        MD5 key: fpacmd5 'node> 3 7 1 12 5 [1795430000]' then the
        password (asked without echo).